        "name": "Escaping",
        "score": 10,
        "rationale": "The term is URL-encoded with `urllib.parse.quote_plus` before going into the href, and the whole URL is then passed through `html.escape`; the visible text uses `html.escape` too, so input like `\"><script>x</script>` or `a&b=c` can't break out of either context."
      },
      {
        "name": "Behavior",
        "score": 10,
        "rationale": "It returns a single anchor pointing at `https://help.example.com/search?q=...` with the visible text `Search the help center for <term>`, and the tests check both the plain case and the hostile-input case."
      },
      {
